Facts you may use: the callback is stored in a ref so that a parent re-rendering with a new inline function does not reset the timer. The cleanup clears the pending timer on unmount, since calling the callback after unmount updates state on an unmounted component. 300 ms matches the search API's guidance for typing.

```ts
export function useDebounced<T>(value: T, onSettle: (value: T) => void, delay = 300) {
  const callback = useRef(onSettle);
  callback.current = onSettle;

  useEffect(() => {
    const timer = setTimeout(() => callback.current(value), delay);
    return () => clearTimeout(timer);
  }, [value, delay]);
}
```
